  m_Name: 21 - While Loop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_while
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: While Loop
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'A <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>while</color></font> loop
    is used to repeat instructions as long as a condition remains true.

    Unlike
    a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color></font> loop, which usually
    repeats a fixed number of times, a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>while</color></font>
    loop continues running until the condition becomes <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#55AAFF>False</color></font>.

    

    Example:

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF">distance <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> <color=#B5CEA8>3</color></font></indent>

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#6A9955># Continue moving while distance is greater than 0</color></font></indent>

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>while</color> distance <color=#D4D4D4>></color> <color=#B5CEA8>0</color><color=#D4D4D4>:</color></font></indent>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>move_forward</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font></indent>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF">distance <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> distance <color=#D4D4D4>-</color> <color=#B5CEA8>1</color></font></indent>

    

    The
    loop checks the condition before each iteration.

    If the condition is <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font>, the instructions inside the loop execute
    again.

    It is important to update the condition properly. Otherwise, the
    loop may continue forever and create an <color=red>infinite loop</color>.'
  isImageBig: 0
